 "notes": "An implicit key is on one line and at most 1024 characters long, counting the quotes. The first key is a space and 1022 letters: it needs quotes, so it is written as 1025 characters. The second is 600 single quotes: single-quoted it is 1202 characters (each quote doubled), but double-quoted it is 602, so either the short form or the explicit `? ` form is right. The third is 1025 letters, which is too long even without quotes. A writer must use the explicit form (or another form of at most 1024 characters) and never write an implicit key that a reader has to refuse. The kit checks the length itself, because a lenient reader accepts a long key.",
